6 3776 1645 3776 L 1920 3776 Q 1997 3776 1997 3718 L 2003 1062 Q 2003 998 1939 998 L 1664 998 z\n\" transform=\"scale(0.015625)\"/></defs><use xlink:href=\"#LibreFranklin-Regular-e2\"/><use xlink:href=\"#LibreFranklin-Regular-82\" transform=\"translate(55.703125 0)\"/><use xlink:href=\"#LibreFranklin-Regular-80\" transform=\"translate(115.609375 0)\"/><use xlink:href=\"#LibreFranklin-Regular-a9\" transform=\"translate(184.40625 0)\"/><use xlink:href=\"#LibreFranklin-Regular-80\" transform=\"translate(205.3125 0)\"/></g></g><g id=\"text_15\"><g style=\"fill: #333333\" transform=\"translate(193.480313 14.928) scale(0.08 -0.08)\"><use xlink:href=\"#LibreFranklin-Regular-e2\"/><use xlink:href=\"#LibreFranklin-Regular-81\" transform=\"translate(55.703125 0)\"/><use xlink:href=\"#LibreFranklin-Regular-88\" transform=\"translate(102.203125 0)\"/><use xlink:href=\"#LibreFranklin-Regular-a9\" transform=\"translate(169 0)\"/><use xlink:href=\"#LibreFranklin-Regular-88\" transform=\"translate(189.90625 0)\"/></g></g><g id=\"text_16\"><g style=\"fill: #333333\" transform=\"translate(263.659979 14.928) scale(0.08 -0.08)\"><defs><path id=\"LibreFranklin-Regular-e3\" d=\"M 3174 2259 Q 3174 2176 3072 2176 L 480 2170 Q 435 2170 416 2189 Q 397 2208 397 2246 L 397 2522 Q 397 2598 454 2598 L 3110 2598 Q 3174 2598 3174 2534 L 3174 2259 z\n\" transform=\"scale(0.015625)\"/></defs><use xlink:href=\"#LibreFranklin-Regular-e3\"/><use xlink:href=\"#LibreFranklin-Regular-86\" transform=\"translate(55.703125 0)\"/><use xlink:href=\"#LibreFranklin-Regular-a9\" transform=\"translate(121.796875 0)\"/><use xlink:href=\"#LibreFranklin-Regular-80\" transform=\"translate(142.703125 0)\"/></g></g><g id=\"text_17\"><g style=\"fill: #333333\" transform=\"translate(330.867146 22.128) scale(0.08 -0.08)\"><use xlink:href=\"#LibreFranklin-Regular-81\"/><use xlink:href=\"#LibreFranklin-Regular-81\" transform=\"translate(46.5 0)\"/><use xlink:href=\"#LibreFranklin-Regular-82\" transform=\"translate(93 0)\"/><use xlink:href=\"#LibreFranklin-Regular-a9\" transform=\"translate(152.90625 0)\"/><use xlink:href=\"#LibreFranklin-Regular-88\" transform=\"translate(173.8125 0)\"/></g></g></g></g><defs><clipPath id=\"pdbe3d5e163\"><rect x=\"30.768437\" y=\"9.768\" width=\"345.96\" height=\"149.688\"/></clipPath></defs></svg>\n","title":"Exhibit 1 · What Greenleaf is worth to Tidewell ($M)","note":null},"answer":"<p>Standalone: $8M × 10 = <b>$80M</b>.</p> <p>Cost synergies: $2M × 10 = $20M. Revenue synergies: $15M × 25% = $3.75M a year; at a 50% chance, $1.875M × 10 = $18.8M. Integration: −$6M.</p> <p>Value to Tidewell: <b>$112.8M</b>, just above the $110M asking price.</p>"},{"q":"So should Tidewell pay $110M?","exhibit":null,"answer":"<p>At $110M Tidewell keeps only $2.8M of the value it creates, and that depends on the uncertain sales synergies. If they don't happen, the deal is worth $94M: <b>Tidewell overpays by $16M</b>.</p> <p><b>So-what:</b> buy, but pay up front only for what Tidewell controls (about $94M), and pay for the sales upside only if it arrives.</p>"},{"q":"How would you structure the offer?","exhibit":null,"answer":"<ul><li><b>Up front: about $94M</b>, the standalone value plus cost savings less integration ($80M + $20M − $6M); open lower, around $88M, to leave room to negotiate</li> <li><b>Earn-out:</b> up to $16M more over three years if Greenleaf's sales through Tidewell's stores reach agreed targets. The sellers reach their $110M only if the sales synergy arrives</li> <li><b>Keep the founders</b> for two years, with part of the earn-out tied to their staying; the brand's appeal is in its founder story</li></ul>"}],"reco":"Buy Greenleaf, but not for $110M up front. On its own it is worth about $80M; certain cost savings add $20M and integration costs $6M, so Tidewell should pay about $94M up front. The extra-sales synergy is worth about $19M but is a coin flip, so pay for it through an earn-out tied to sales targets. Total value to Tidewell is about $113M, so offering $110M up front would hand almost all of it to the sellers. Risk: losing the founders, so tie part of the earn-out to their staying.","great":["Values the target on its own first","Separates certain cost synergies from uncertain revenue synergies","Sets a walk-away price","Uses deal structure (earn-out) to share risk"],"id":63,"slug":"tidewell-foods"}